.SH SECURITY & FUZZING
.SS Historical Vulnerability Fixes
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAPL (TYPE 42) afdlength Stack Buffer Overflow (CWE-121 / CWE-787)\fR:
\fBformat_rdata_for_display()\fR (used during \fB+yaml\fR formatting and
\fB+allcompare\fR record hash calculation) copied \fBafdlength\fR bytes into a
fixed \fBuint8_t addr[16]\fR buffer without upper-bound clamping. Fixed by
clamping copy length: \fBcopy_len = (afdlength > sizeof(addr)) ? sizeof(addr) :
afdlength;\fR and emitting a diagnostic indicator \fB[APL afdlength=%u invalid
for AFI=%u]\fR. Regression testing is automated via
\fBtests/run_dag_apl_afdlength_overflow_test.sh\fR and continuous fuzzer
\fBtests/fuzz/fuzz_dag_hash\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\fB+trace\fB CNAME Tracking Stack Exhaustion via Deep Recursion (CWE-674 /
CWE-789)\fR: \fBrun_trace_query_impl()\fR recursively invoked itself up to
\fBTRACE_MAX_CNAME_DEPTH\fR (16) times when traversing CNAME delegation
chains. Each recursive frame allocated ~270 KB of stack buffers
(\fBroot_qbuf\fR, \fBroot_resp\fR, \fBqbuf\fR, \fBresp\fR at 65,535 bytes each
plus local arrays), consuming up to 4.3 MB of stack under unoptimized
(\fB\-O0\fR) or instrumented (ASan/TSan) builds where Tail Call Optimization
(TCO) is inhibited. Fixed by converting the CNAME resolution into an iterative
loop (\fBcname_depth\fR loop) and allocating the four 65 KB I/O buffers on the
heap with guaranteed cleanup, reducing per-call stack usage to a single ~16 KB
frame. Since then \fB+trace\fR no longer follows CNAMEs at all (it stops at the
CNAME answer like BIND \fBdig\fR 9.20; chains are followed by \fB+trace2\fR,
which bounds them at 16 links and detects loops). Regression testing is
automated via \fBtests/run_dag_trace_deep_cname_stack_test.sh\fR.
.SS Fuzzing & Differential Test Harnesses
